A||N||12||Monkeyman||Some engine problems--Help||||1||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||01:07 PM||||'85 GT w/ a touch over 72k miles.  At idle (when it's warmed up), the idle hunts.  I understand that Fieros tend to do that, but as the idle drops, the car starts to shake slightly (as if it was going to die, but never does).  Also, I don't get much power at lower rpms.  Once I top 2500 or so, I can feel a definite increase in power.  Is this normal?<P>I've replaced the fuel filter and the cat can't be clogged since it doesn't have one.  The only other thing my mechanically challenged mind can think of is that the car is rebelling since I haven't named her yet.  I talked really sweet to her, touched her where her bra would be, massaged her tailpipe, etc, etc to no avail.  What's next??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||03-27-2001||01:25 PM||||Washer fluid?  Sorry.<BR>Check the IAC valve?  If it's sticking or not working, your idle will be erratic.<P>Has it had the basic tune up stuff?  Plugs, cap, rotor, wires, etc?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||01:32 PM||||Haven't checked the IAC yet, but figured the idle and lack of low end power might be from the same cause.  All of the normal tune up stuff has been done recently except new plugs.  I guess that's next.  Hopefully that will help some.<P>BTW--The washer fluid is fine.  Just topped it off last night.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||03-27-2001||01:33 PM||||TPS ?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||02:32 PM||||Just changed it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Lewis||03-27-2001||02:44 PM||||I had a idle problem when I first got my 85gt.  The car would stall after warm up at an idle.  Someone suggested I clean out the throttle body with cleaner.  The throttle body was very dirty and a lot of black gunk came out.  The problem I was having at the time was cured.  Hope this helps..<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||03:07 PM||||Wasn't the throttle body on the 2.5?||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||03-27-2001||03:21 PM||||Both 4 and 6 have them, Dave.  On the 6, it's the aluminum section between the plenum and the intake hose leading to the air filter canister.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||03-27-2001||03:25 PM||||Thanx, Scott.  I'll have to check that out this weekend.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||lou_dias||03-27-2001||03:55 PM||||might also be a misfiring cylinder||||reg||1
Z||000010||WisconsinGT||03-27-2001||06:06 PM||||Hey! I have a similer problem on my 88 2.8. regarding the idle. I just got off the phone with the GM guy who says, my #4 cylinder is dead. Well, he mentioned that at around 2500 rpm's it smooths out. So, I think you might want to check into that. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Taijiguy||03-27-2001||06:13 PM||||Hey Monkeyman, mine runs OK, must just be your car. :P||||reg||1
